WEBVTT

00:11.640 --> 00:14.870
<i>Banshee, this is Echo 1. How do you read? Banshee?</i>

00:15.280 --> 00:18.490
<i>Second attack! Large number of SAMs!</i>

00:18.510 --> 00:20.780
<i>What's the deal, Banshee?! We're friendlies!</i>

00:20.780 --> 00:23.020
<i>God dammit! No response!</i>

00:23.020 --> 00:26.760
<i>Alpha 4's been shot down! IFF has no response!</i>

00:26.760 --> 00:29.020
<i>Echo 4 and Echo 7 have been shot down!</i>

00:29.020 --> 00:30.960
<i>Close defense system is...</i>

00:30.960 --> 00:34.260
<i>God dammit! Eject! Eject! Eject!</i>

01:44.040 --> 01:44.940
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

01:45.170 --> 01:52.560
Battle Fairy

01:45.170 --> 01:52.560
YUKIKAZE

01:55.380 --> 01:56.320
"Assuming?"

01:58.210 --> 02:03.100
By "assuming," are you saying you don't believe in the JAM's existence?!

02:03.490 --> 02:06.560
Oh, no. I don't mean that.

02:06.560 --> 02:12.090
However, well... The fact is that, as things stand now,

02:12.090 --> 02:16.660
the public doesn't really believe the reports we get from the UN or the FAF.

02:17.770 --> 02:22.530
At the very least, they don't think it has a direct impact on our day-to-day life.

02:22.940 --> 02:26.010
So, Ms. Jackson-san, that's why your book is...

02:26.010 --> 02:28.000
Selling, right?

02:28.610 --> 02:30.840
As a well-realized work of fiction.

02:31.310 --> 02:33.910
You can look at it that way, too, I mean.

02:34.880 --> 02:39.750
By the way, is it true Hollywood wants to make it into a movie?

02:41.960 --> 02:44.480
Pardon me. Could we wrap this up, please?

02:45.190 --> 02:46.920
You have another appointment?

02:46.930 --> 02:49.090
Yes. More research to gather.

02:50.400 --> 02:52.730
Down south a bit. You know?

02:57.270 --> 02:58.360
I'm coming in.

03:00.580 --> 03:03.810
Oh, Capt. Foss. What is it?

03:04.510 --> 03:06.010
You called me, Major.

03:06.920 --> 03:07.920
I did?

03:08.550 --> 03:10.750
The one I called for was Lt. Fukai.

03:11.220 --> 03:12.320
Yes.

03:12.320 --> 03:15.410
You called for Lt. Fukai during a counseling session.

03:15.960 --> 03:19.500
My sessions are conducted according to his treatment program.

03:19.730 --> 03:22.050
That's why I must object to this sort of thing!

03:22.930 --> 03:26.700
The lieutenant himself is uncooperative during our exams as it is!

03:29.070 --> 03:31.010
He's been ordered on a mission.

03:31.970 --> 03:35.270
If you have any problems with that, take them up with Gen. Cooly.

03:36.380 --> 03:38.900
Banshee 4 has apparently gone berserk.

03:39.620 --> 03:43.430
They lost control of all systems suddenly, without explanation.

03:45.190 --> 03:49.560
It then wiped out an entire squadron of friendly units on their way back to base.

03:51.060 --> 03:55.900
We have a Minx trailing it right now, but it's not responding to any of our calls.

03:53.160 --> 03:55.730
<i>This is FAF unit Minx, calling Banshee 4.</i>

03:55.880 --> 03:56.920
<i>Banshee, please respond.</i>

03:57.070 --> 04:00.900
We believe that there are still quite a number of crewman aboard it, but...

04:01.090 --> 04:02.970
<i>Banshee! Banshee, respond!</i>

04:02.970 --> 04:07.760
As you know, the two Banshees we have are vital to our air defense here on Fairy.

04:08.710 --> 04:14.620
If we lose one, half of the FAF will be left naked.

04:15.520 --> 04:16.500
Is it the JAM?

04:18.320 --> 04:20.120
We still don't know.

04:24.590 --> 04:30.190
Apparently, the Systems Corps is sending an engineer out to investigate the cause of the failure.

04:31.230 --> 04:35.290
Your job is to be his combination bodyguard and chauffeur.

04:37.010 --> 04:39.010
Well, that's the reason.

04:39.010 --> 04:41.130
It's nothing personal against you, Captain.

04:50.520 --> 04:53.980
The report we got about that frontline base.

04:54.920 --> 04:58.650
Seems it was destroyed a while ago in a surprise raid.

04:59.560 --> 05:02.480
You made direct contact with the JAM.

05:04.000 --> 05:07.030
You may be the first Earth man who ever has.

05:08.270 --> 05:10.640
Now, consider our situation since then...

05:11.770 --> 05:13.450
<i>Engine trouble!</i>

05:13.450 --> 05:15.640
<i>No good! It won't recognize it!</i>

05:17.610 --> 05:19.610
Sabotage by the JAM.

05:19.610 --> 05:25.210
No, worse. There's talk that the JAM have infiltrated the FAF itself.

05:25.550 --> 05:27.720
It's practically got us in a panic.

05:29.560 --> 05:33.220
In contrast, the folks back on Earth couldn't care less.

05:36.160 --> 05:40.190
While we're here fighting and close to nervous breakdowns...

05:41.700 --> 05:44.250
...they wonder if the JAM are even real.

05:53.280 --> 05:56.180
It's flying, but your target is still an aircraft carrier.

05:56.180 --> 05:58.120
You should have no trouble landing.

05:59.960 --> 06:03.320
Just to be safe, though, we're fitting wire anchors to your plane.

06:03.890 --> 06:07.100
There's one other new toy we've given you...

06:07.100 --> 06:09.090
Hm? What's wrong?

06:14.900 --> 06:16.200
Rei, wait!

06:21.610 --> 06:22.770
What are you doing?

06:26.210 --> 06:27.530
Get out!

06:27.880 --> 06:30.180
Um, sure. Sorry.

06:31.750 --> 06:35.450
I was just confirming the mission data they're sending us, that's all.

06:36.020 --> 06:38.890
Hey! That's a superior officer you just yelled at!

06:39.070 --> 06:40.440
Allow me to introduce you.

06:41.430 --> 06:46.050
This is Capt. Tom John of the Systems Corps, who will be accompanying you to Banshee.

06:46.440 --> 06:49.810
And this is the pilot of Unit 3, Yukikaze.

06:49.810 --> 06:51.710
1st Lieutenant Rei Fukai.

06:53.240 --> 06:55.230
It's a pleasure, Lieutenant.

07:01.980 --> 07:03.350
Feeling better, Captain?

07:03.990 --> 07:05.710
I'm fine.

07:06.150 --> 07:09.950
I'm here because I couldn't leave Banshee's systems in someone else's hands.

07:10.760 --> 07:13.590
The captain specializes in avionics.

07:14.360 --> 07:17.820
Yukikaze's systems are his handiwork, too.

07:19.230 --> 07:20.460
Yukikaze's...?

07:20.490 --> 07:22.560
Hardly my "handiwork."

07:22.970 --> 07:25.290
Just a small part of them.

07:26.480 --> 07:27.650
You...

07:28.880 --> 07:31.150
I'm just an engineer.

07:31.150 --> 07:34.950
I mean, I went out on a test flight the other day, and look what happened to me!

07:44.530 --> 07:46.770
A JAM sensor jammer!

07:46.770 --> 07:49.420
I've never seen one actually mounted on a plane before!

07:49.870 --> 07:51.800
That's the warning pattern.

07:52.870 --> 07:56.040
Well, it's still in the prototype stage.

07:56.040 --> 07:59.770
But we don't know what's going to happen out there, so just in case.

08:00.440 --> 08:01.620
Hm? What's wrong?

08:03.650 --> 08:05.880
They disguise themselves as Sylphs.

08:06.680 --> 08:08.620
Now we pretend to be JAM, huh?

08:09.180 --> 08:10.910
Damn straight.

08:12.680 --> 08:14.110
A vicious cycle.

08:30.010 --> 08:32.430
I'm to monitor his behavior on the mission?

08:33.310 --> 08:37.870
Yes. Ask the major for more details.

08:38.680 --> 08:41.670
We've never done anything like this before, but...

08:43.820 --> 08:47.190
General. Call for you on line one.

08:48.760 --> 08:49.820
Cooly here.

08:50.330 --> 08:52.590
Ah, Colonel.

08:53.330 --> 08:55.380
Yes, of course.

08:57.000 --> 09:00.560
This was a job that we should've been handling, but...

09:02.040 --> 09:04.890
Right. I hope this won't be too much trouble for you.

09:06.270 --> 09:08.940
Yes, and please be sure we get any intel from the site.

09:09.880 --> 09:11.440
Yes, ma'am. Later, then.

09:14.280 --> 09:16.450
She's a sly one...

09:16.450 --> 09:20.870
<i>B-3, taxi to runway 22 via Alpha Papa 4.</i>

09:20.910 --> 09:21.590
<i>Roger.</i>

09:21.590 --> 09:23.360
From here?

09:23.360 --> 09:27.290
This is a top secret investigation.
Did you bring the application for an analysis?

09:28.260 --> 09:31.790
I can start it up with this. Who's my subject?

09:32.700 --> 09:35.550
Those two men... And Yukikaze.

09:37.340 --> 09:39.670
You want me to psychoanalyze a fighter plane?!

09:40.610 --> 09:43.390
Yukikaze is not an ordinary machine.

09:44.650 --> 09:48.730
It possesses a high degree of intelligence. Combat intelligence, so to speak.

09:50.120 --> 09:55.350
Just like the other computers in the FAF, right?

10:04.370 --> 10:05.730
Tomahawk?

10:05.730 --> 10:08.500
Yeah, that's what everyone calls me.

10:09.740 --> 10:12.170
But, I don't mind it.

10:12.170 --> 10:13.600
How do I put it...?

10:14.040 --> 10:17.100
It makes me feel brave, somehow.

10:18.880 --> 10:21.350
There are JAM in the FAF?!

10:21.680 --> 10:26.090
Yeah. But the thing is, we're not entirely sure what they're disguised as.

10:26.090 --> 10:28.700
What did the Central Computer have to say about it?

10:29.320 --> 10:32.790
"Insufficient data." Please continue analysis.

10:35.230 --> 10:39.600
It's beautiful! It's like a tourist-spot around here!

10:39.600 --> 10:42.820
Are you nuts? This is a battlefield.

10:42.830 --> 10:44.800
Well, I guess so.

10:45.810 --> 10:48.610
I've been sort of a coward, ever since I was little.

10:48.610 --> 10:50.690
My grandpa used to say that all the time.

10:51.680 --> 10:56.980
How his father, his grandfather and all our ancestors had been brave warriors.

10:57.590 --> 11:00.850
"So," he'd tell me, "you are one, too."

11:02.490 --> 11:05.180
But... I just couldn't...

11:06.460 --> 11:10.300
I never liked fighting with other people.

11:15.770 --> 11:18.240
Seems to be scared of something...

11:18.970 --> 11:20.110
Tom John?

11:20.440 --> 11:23.100
No, Yukikaze.

11:26.580 --> 11:30.050
A war between the JAM and our machines, huh?

11:30.050 --> 11:31.610
Have you read that book?

11:31.990 --> 11:36.540
Yeah. It mentions some good things, but...

11:37.460 --> 11:40.590
Nobody on Earth could understand.

11:43.160 --> 11:45.760
I hope we can make the JAM feel like you do.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.370
On Banshee, you mean?

11:47.370 --> 11:50.730
No way! It's gotta be just a systems error.

11:53.780 --> 11:55.540
We'll know soon enough.

11:58.350 --> 12:03.750
<i>B-6 to B-3. Aside from the lack of contact, we can't spot any problems.</i>

12:03.750 --> 12:05.220
<i>Still, watch your step.</i>

12:05.220 --> 12:07.320
<i>Bingo fuel. RTB.</i>

12:07.320 --> 12:09.310
B-3, roger.

12:11.160 --> 12:14.290
My God...! That thing's enormous!

12:15.200 --> 12:17.030
I've got a bad feeling about this.

12:17.030 --> 12:18.900
It's too quiet.

12:18.900 --> 12:23.330
C'mon, you're over thinking this. There's nothing out of the ordinary, anywhere.

12:25.570 --> 12:27.830
First off, we'd better land on it.

12:28.410 --> 12:30.040
I know.

12:31.710 --> 12:34.150
IFF check, complete.

12:35.320 --> 12:38.110
Clearance, okay. Check number.

12:38.550 --> 12:40.110
He's on approach.

12:42.960 --> 12:44.690
Gate, open.

12:44.690 --> 12:46.560
Gear, down and locked.

12:47.100 --> 12:49.240
Meatball, in sight.

12:50.500 --> 12:54.250
Catch arm... Up and ready.

13:00.780 --> 13:02.500
Landing, complete.

13:06.180 --> 13:08.780
B-3, now fully stopped.

13:25.300 --> 13:26.510
Okay, let's get to work.

13:28.940 --> 13:30.380
What was that all about?

13:31.140 --> 13:33.370
It's just a dolly, isn't it?

13:39.350 --> 13:40.490
Know how to use it?

13:41.280 --> 13:44.480
Come on... I don't need this.

13:45.320 --> 13:47.380
First, we go to the bridge.

13:51.530 --> 13:53.050
Hey! Wait!

13:53.760 --> 13:55.820
Lieutenant, wait for me!

14:24.060 --> 14:26.260
Quiet, isn't it?

14:26.260 --> 14:28.460
You wouldn't think we were flying at all.

14:30.330 --> 14:34.100
They're old, but Banshee's engines are well-made.

14:35.440 --> 14:37.270
Just like my heart.

14:39.640 --> 14:42.740
Oh, yeah. I have an artificial heart.

14:43.110 --> 14:44.730
Plutonium-powered.

14:45.580 --> 14:50.480
There are certain countries I can't enter because of this heart.

14:52.590 --> 14:54.820
Funny, isn't it?

14:54.820 --> 14:59.090
Even though the electricity they live with is generated by nuclear power.

15:00.700 --> 15:04.320
Don't be bothered with people like that.

15:12.070 --> 15:13.910
Maybe that's the reason...

15:13.910 --> 15:17.600
The reason why I've always been so interested in mechanisms and systems.

15:18.910 --> 15:23.320
Every machine contains the ideals of the ones who built it.

15:24.950 --> 15:26.290
That's what I think, anyway.

15:30.530 --> 15:31.390
Even Yukikaze?

15:31.990 --> 15:33.830
Well, that...

15:33.830 --> 15:36.020
The Mave is special.

15:37.030 --> 15:41.440
It's a special model, made with the skills and experiences of the STC and the SAF people.

15:41.440 --> 15:44.500
It went beyond being an ordinary machine.

15:46.740 --> 15:47.410
But...

15:50.110 --> 15:53.310
You, the one who flies it... are human, right?

15:57.520 --> 15:59.850
I detect transient shared consciousness...

15:59.850 --> 16:02.020
...along with sympathy.

16:04.490 --> 16:05.600
I don't feel that way.

16:06.250 --> 16:08.900
No. I meant Lt. Fukai.

16:10.830 --> 16:12.530
Of course.

16:13.230 --> 16:15.110
They're arriving on the bridge.

16:18.070 --> 16:19.180
Nobody's home.

16:19.820 --> 16:23.470
They probably evacuated because such a large error took them by surprise.

16:25.750 --> 16:29.300
They're probably getting rained on in the jungle somewhere.

16:30.350 --> 16:33.360
Looks like the computer room's above us.

16:33.450 --> 16:35.660
I'll go see if I can debug it.

16:35.660 --> 16:37.930
That's why I came, after all.

16:37.930 --> 16:39.430
How about you, Lieutenant?

16:59.510 --> 17:02.920
Oh, hi, Lieutenant. Yeah, I just got started.

17:03.420 --> 17:05.680
Huh? Inside the carrier?

17:06.350 --> 17:08.650
Sure. Roger that.

17:09.060 --> 17:11.170
Don't worry about me here.

17:11.490 --> 17:13.590
Yeah. Talk to you later.

17:21.800 --> 17:23.000
Yukikaze...

17:34.280 --> 17:35.950
That should do it... Whoa!

17:45.560 --> 17:47.800
Banshee 4, accelerating!

17:47.800 --> 17:49.210
It's altering course.

17:49.660 --> 17:51.970
Changing to a heading of 0-2-6.

17:51.970 --> 17:55.630
Probability it will breach our absolute air defense perimeter: 93%!

17:56.940 --> 17:59.700
Distance to defensive missile corps's trip line...

18:00.340 --> 18:01.550
500 kilometers!

18:05.180 --> 18:07.520
The STC's ordered them to fire?!

18:08.180 --> 18:11.550
Hold on! We've still got an investigation underway in there...

18:11.630 --> 18:14.610
What?! You can't cancel it?!

18:15.060 --> 18:16.570
Bullshit!

18:17.260 --> 18:20.530
Get me a comm line! We have to contact Lt. Fukai at once!

18:21.770 --> 18:23.320
I thought this was top secret.

18:23.930 --> 18:25.070
Hurry!

18:25.070 --> 18:26.290
Yes, sir!

18:27.140 --> 18:28.290
Hey! Rei!

18:29.440 --> 18:32.210
Rei, do you read me? Rei!

18:53.660 --> 18:55.820
Come in! Rei!

18:57.000 --> 19:00.400
You gotta bug out of there! They're launching an SRBM!

19:01.000 --> 19:02.230
Dammit!

19:03.740 --> 19:06.120
I'm not getting through! What's the problem?!

19:06.480 --> 19:10.200
<i>I- It looks like they've gone into a magnetically-charged thunder bank, sir!</i>

19:10.210 --> 19:12.480
<i>Just get me through to them! I don't care how!</i>

19:12.480 --> 19:16.500
Y- Yes, sir! I'll try boosting the directivity of the SSW!

19:19.650 --> 19:24.130
<i>Rei, do you read me? Banshee's changed course.</i>

19:24.130 --> 19:27.640
<i>If you read me, answer at once! Rei!</i>

19:29.530 --> 19:30.890
Jack!

19:31.230 --> 19:35.940
<i>Rei! You're all right? Listen, you've gotta get out of there at once!</i>

19:35.940 --> 19:37.560
<i>Where's Tom John?</i>

19:38.370 --> 19:42.640
The JAM have consumed Banshee's crew... No, it's...!

19:42.670 --> 19:45.040
Right now...! What?

19:46.270 --> 19:47.110
What did you say?!

19:51.450 --> 19:54.750
They're... copying humans here...!

20:04.370 --> 20:05.460
Copies?!

20:05.870 --> 20:09.180
They're duplicating humans...?

20:10.710 --> 20:12.350
My God...

20:13.910 --> 20:15.940
Tom! Emergency!

20:16.180 --> 20:19.170
Stop your work! I'll meet you in the hangar bay!

20:20.750 --> 20:22.110
Capt. Foss!

20:23.450 --> 20:24.190
Yes, sir?

20:24.520 --> 20:25.670
Forget it...

20:26.090 --> 20:29.200
Submit search request to the STC.

20:29.860 --> 20:30.700
Yes, sir.

20:31.230 --> 20:33.250
Condition is as follows:

20:35.200 --> 20:38.130
"Regarding the sabotage within the FAF,"

20:39.130 --> 20:43.590
"assuming the JAM have been copying humans."

20:50.180 --> 20:51.370
Tom!

20:51.680 --> 20:53.560
Why won't you respond?

20:54.550 --> 20:56.310
Response from STC.

20:57.180 --> 20:59.490
"Assuming a plan to copy humans,"

20:59.490 --> 21:03.360
"those who would be useful to them would be as follows:"

21:05.060 --> 21:07.320
"Airplane crash victims..."

21:07.860 --> 21:10.330
<i>Seems to be scared of something...</i>

21:11.000 --> 21:13.290
<i>That's the warning pattern.</i>

21:14.140 --> 21:19.700
"Those who have been to the front lines, where they were cut off from contact with others for a period of time..."

21:20.780 --> 21:21.500
Tom.

21:26.080 --> 21:28.050
What did you say?!

21:28.750 --> 21:32.850
"Additionally, personnel correlating to given data..."

21:33.050 --> 21:36.560
"...who are currently involved in the SAF are the following two:"

21:36.920 --> 21:40.990
"5th Squadron, unit 3 pilot, Lt. Rei Fukai..."

21:41.600 --> 21:44.760
"...and Capt. Tom John of the Systems Corps...!"

21:47.670 --> 21:49.370
Get away from there! Tom!

21:54.340 --> 21:55.930
It's a JAM!

21:56.380 --> 21:57.670
Don't you understand?!

22:04.790 --> 22:06.970
What was that just now?

22:08.190 --> 22:09.680
Where...?

22:14.830 --> 22:16.450
They knew.

22:16.800 --> 22:19.560
That's why they had us following their moves?

22:30.510 --> 22:36.200
Rei, be careful! Tom lost contact with us once during his test flight!

22:36.820 --> 22:39.050
All things considered...

22:39.450 --> 22:43.460
...I think he may be a copy the JAM have created!

22:44.290 --> 22:45.410
I...

22:45.790 --> 22:49.020
I... What was I doing here with that thing?!

22:49.960 --> 22:51.890
Please tell me, Lieutenant!

22:52.170 --> 22:55.620
Why was I here with a JAM?!

22:59.710 --> 23:00.670
We're going back.

23:01.240 --> 23:02.870
Lieutenant...

23:03.540 --> 23:04.650
Why?

23:05.550 --> 23:07.910
It's my duty to bring you back.

23:09.710 --> 23:10.600
That's all.

23:12.320 --> 23:13.530
You...

23:19.530 --> 23:21.650
SRBM, launching.

23:24.400 --> 23:27.200
Time to target: 8 minutes, 32 seconds.

24:03.570 --> 24:07.130
SRBM will reach target in 6 minutes!

24:26.740 --> 24:27.390
Got it...

24:38.010 --> 24:39.540
Okay, let's go, Tom!

24:55.960 --> 24:56.930
Tom!

24:57.260 --> 24:59.510
What's wrong? Hurry! Get in!

25:00.630 --> 25:02.960
You really are a good man.

25:03.960 --> 25:05.020
What are you saying?!

25:08.440 --> 25:10.650
Stop the lift! Get in!

25:11.570 --> 25:13.860
Goodbye, Lieutenant.

25:15.340 --> 25:16.780
Tomahawk...!

25:30.960 --> 25:32.870
I thought the people in the SAF...

25:33.590 --> 25:38.300
...were colder-hearted, like machines.

25:50.170 --> 25:53.810
But still, I guess you really are human.

26:01.020 --> 26:05.820
I don't want to have a heart like ice forever...

26:20.110 --> 26:21.420
I am...

26:35.420 --> 26:36.400
<i>I am...</i>

26:39.460 --> 26:44.860
<i>After B-3 ramps in, all ground crew shall hang it and check.</i>

26:45.240 --> 26:50.830
<i>After B-3 ramps in, all ground crew shall hang it and check.</i>

27:02.880 --> 27:03.940
<i>I am...</i>

27:06.850 --> 27:08.500
<i>I am human, aren't I?</i>

27:27.680 --> 27:32.680
In my dreams, it comes so clearly.

27:34.090 --> 27:39.850
Letting me embrace that day.

27:42.260 --> 27:47.130
I've seen a lot of summers off...

27:48.600 --> 27:54.830
...along the way to now.

27:56.170 --> 27:58.770
Long way to home.

27:58.570 --> 28:02.570
Because I love your smile...

28:02.440 --> 28:09.010
...that never changes.

28:10.580 --> 28:13.250
Long way to home.

